% Decisions of the Medicare Appeals Council on supplies — surgical dressings
% (surgical_dressings.le, LCD L33831 with Policy Article A54563) and a
% disposable insulin delivery system (external_infusion_pumps.le, LCD L33794
% with Policy Article A52507); the glucose monitor policy
% (glucose_monitors.le) is included because the insulin system's controller
% is coded as a home glucose monitor. Each policy includes dmepos.le (orders,
% delivery, benefit category, continued need, refills).
%
% One scenario per decision, named after its text file in sources/council/
% ("scenario couriermed is, as stated in Council decision couriermed:"),
% written as council_pmd.le and council_other.le write theirs: each fact
% quotes its passage ("confer \"...\""), the treating practitioner's findings
% say "according to the treating practitioner", the Council's "according to
% the Council" with the reason it gave. The Council's outcome is NOT a fact:
% it is in the comment above each scenario; the expectation is what the
% model derives, and where it differs the comment says DISAGREES and why.
%
% The dressing decisions apply the surgical dressings LCDs of 2008-2011
% (L11449, L11460, L11471) and their Policy Articles (A23903, A24114,
% A23664), whose criteria for each product type are, in substance, those of
% today's L33831; three of their grounds are not in the model: the
% documentation the Council demanded beyond the supplier's order and
% evaluation forms (a daily or weekly clinical course of the wound: the
% model reads the wound's characteristics as facts, and a decision that
% states none leaves every criterion unmet); the end-stage renal disease
% composite rate, which pays for the dressings of a dialysis access catheter
% (in today's Article A54563, and not in surgical_dressings.le); and the
% partial allowance of a claim (the Council allows the usual quantity and
% denies the excess, the model decides a claim as a whole). The dressing
% decisions are sample or multi-beneficiary cases: a scenario transcribes the
% claims the Council names, and says which it leaves out.
%
% Codes: the decisions cite the codes of their day, which are today's except
% the borderless composite dressings A6200 and A6201, deleted in 2008 and
% transcribed as billed (no policy decides them: the claim is outside the
% model's scope). Where a decision names no code for a claim, the one
% assumed is said in the comment. Facts the vocabulary cannot express are
% listed in each comment as candidate templates.

the target language is: prolog.
scenario facts require provenance.

the knowledge base council supplies includes these resources:
    surgical_dressings,
    external_infusion_pumps,
    glucose_monitors.

the knowledge base council supplies includes:

